-- title:
--   Fixer of the Γ₀(M) function field lies in ±Γ₀(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $K$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure, let $t\in K$, and let $\sigma:\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})\to \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{C}}(K)$ be a group homomorphism whose kernel is $\Gamma(M)\vee\langle -1\rangle$; assume $K$ is finite and Galois over the subfield $\mathbb{C}\langle t\rangle$ generated by $t$, of degree equal to the index of $\Gamma(M)\vee\langle -1\rangle$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $F$ denote the intermediate field `laurentBaseChange` of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise image of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M)`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of pairs of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_0(M)$ with nonzero denominator. Fix a ring embedding $\iota:\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\mathbb{C}$, a ring homomorphism $\Phi:F\to K$, and a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra map $E':K\to\mathbb{C}((q))$ with $E'(t)$ the series `jqModC` for $j$ read in $q^M$, and $E'(\Phi u)$ the $\iota$-image of $u$ read in $q^M$ for all $u\in F$. Assume there is $y_0\in F$ whose underlying series is `jqModC` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\Phi y_0=t$, and that every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ fixes $\Phi u$ for all $u$. Then any $\delta\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\sigma\delta$ fixing $\Phi u$ for all $u$ lies in $\Gamma_0(M)\vee\langle -1\rangle$.
--
--   This is the Galois-theoretic identification of $\pm\Gamma_0(M)$ as the exact stabiliser of the image of the function field of $X_0(M)$ inside the function field of $X(M)$, the inclusion opposite to the evident invariance; the degree computation [`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqModC_laurentBaseChange_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma0_eq_index`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqModC_laurentBaseChange_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma0_eq_index) supplies the matching index. It is used in the analysis of orders of vanishing and of ramification indices for the maps between the modular curves $X(M)$, $X_0(M)$ and $X_H$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LevelN_Descent_fixer_le_gamma0.lean

